      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "Previous LTPA-focussed research has mostly been quantified by time, frequency, and/or intensity (e.g., light intensity, moderate-vigorous intensity), with little investigation into the impact of the specific activity types of LTPA being performed [12-15]. The World Health Organisation Physical Activity and Sedentary Behaviour Guidelines Development Group [14] identified understanding the health effects of different PA types as one of four major evidence gaps in current knowledge.",
      "reason": "The introduction explicitly describes the current state of knowledge (research mostly quantified by time/frequency/intensity) and identifies important uncertainties (little investigation into specific activity types)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "Therefore, summarising the current state of knowledge of the longitudinal health and behavioural effects of specific LTPA types could help inform public health policy and direct future research.",
      "reason": "The text explains the importance and need for the review by stating it will inform public health policy and direct future research."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "Previous systematic reviews have highlighted the influence of activity structure and type on psychosocial outcomes in children [22] and cardiovascular health in adults [23]. Another review identified a largely positive relationship between overall childhood sport participation and adulthood PA [24]. However, the longitudinal associations between participation in specific LTPA types during childhood and adolescence and adult health and PA behaviours remains unknown.",
      "reason": "The text cites previous systematic reviews ([22], [23], [24]) and explains the need for the current review by highlighting the remaining uncertainty regarding specific LTPA types."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This is a systematic review of observational studies examining associations between physical activity participation and health outcomes, not an intervention review. Therefore, describing a mechanism of action for an intervention is not applicable."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This is a systematic review of observational studies, not a review of complex interventions. Therefore, considering a logic model for intervention components is not applicable."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 95
}

